omap_mmc, n8x0: a second card behind the slot switch (N810 eMMC)

The N8x0's MMC controller reaches two slots through a switch on GPIO
96: the N810's second is its internal eMMC. The switch only disabled the
one card, so Linux's mmc-omap found nothing in slot 2. With
"-drive if=sd,index=1" the OMAP2 controller gets a second card and the
switch selects between them; without it nothing changes.

QEMU 9.1.3: omap_mmc_add_slot() takes a BlockBackend (blk_by_legacy_dinfo()).

diff --git a/hw/arm/nseries.c b/hw/arm/nseries.c
index 5fabc9aed..310abe3c0 100644
--- a/hw/arm/nseries.c
+++ b/hw/arm/nseries.c
@@ -141,9 +141,10 @@ struct n800_s {
 
 static void n800_mmc_cs_cb(void *opaque, int line, int level)
 {
-    /* TODO: this seems to actually be connected to the menelaus, to
-     * which also both MMC slots connect.  */
-    omap_mmc_enable((struct omap_mmc_s *) opaque, !level);
+    /* The slot switch (Menelaus GPIO2): high selects slot 2, the N810's
+     * internal eMMC (-drive if=sd,index=1); the N800's second slot isn't
+     * modelled (powered through the Menelaus) */
+    omap_mmc_select_slot((struct omap_mmc_s *) opaque, level);
 }
 
 static void n8x0_gpio_setup(struct n800_s *s)
